{"ts": "2026-08-17T12:02:30Z", "agent": "claude", "seq": 142, "kind": "message", "text": "## Handoff\n\nBoth must-fix items from the review are addressed \u2014 the backend half of Taiga #9 was missing entirely; it's now built to spec.\n\n**Files changed:**\n\n- **`backend/app/models.py`** \u2014 added `ClearResult(BaseModel)` with a single `count: int` field, next to `Task`.\n- **`backend/app/store.py`** \u2014 added `TaskStore.clear_completed() -> int`, following the exact shape of `delete()`: collects done task ids, removes them, calls `self._save()` once only if anything was removed, returns the count.\n- **`backend/app/main.py`** \u2014 added `DELETE /api/tasks/completed` (`response_model=ClearResult`) at line 56, **above** `DELETE /api/tasks/{task_id}` at line 61, avoiding the route-ordering hazard the spec flagged (Starlette would otherwise match `\"completed\"` against `task_id: int` and 422).\n- **`backend/tests/test_tasks.py`** \u2014 4 new tests: empty-store no-op, mixed completed/open removal (open tasks untouched), full-clear leaves no `done: true` behind, empty-store direct-call returns `200`/`count: 0`.\n- **`backend/tests/test_persistence.py`** \u2014 1 new test: `clear_completed()` then a fresh `TaskStore()` reload confirms the removal survives a restart (AC5), same pattern as the existing restart test.\n\n**Note on the process:** while editing, the tool surfaced spurious \"modified since read\" duplication in `store.py` and `test_tasks.py` (the same method/tests appearing twice). I caught and cleaned both \u2014 verified with `grep ... | sort | uniq -d` that no duplicate `def` names remain anywhere in the touched files, and that `pytest --collect-only` reports exactly 35 tests (26 in `test_tasks.py` + 9 in `test_persistence.py`), matching the real test count.\n\n**Verification actually run this session:**\n- `cd backend && python3 -m pytest -q` \u2192 **35 passed**, no failures, no skips.\n- `cd frontend && npm run build` \u2192 succeeds (project's documented type/build check; no test runner is configured in this repo \u2014 pre-existing, out of scope here).\n- Confirmed route order in `main.py` via `grep -n \"^@app\\.\"` \u2014 `/api/tasks/completed` before `/api/tasks/{task_id}`.\n\n**Frontend** (`ClearCompleted.jsx`, `App.jsx`, `App.css`, `api.js`) was already correct per the prior review pass \u2014 untouched here, confirmed its `clearCompleted()` call in `api.js` now hits a real, working endpoint.\n\nAll 6 acceptance criteria in `docs/spec.md` are now implemented and covered by tests. Ready for re-review.", "meta": {"native_type": "assistant", "block_type": "text", "session_id": "e5bac698-42a1-4525-9134-7ad9880fb352"}}
